.\"                                      Hey, EMACS: -*- nroff -*-
.TH MLNX\-BF\-HUGEPAGES 8 "2026-10-15"
.SH NAME
mlnx\-bf\-hugepages \- configure DOCA hugepages from a system configuration file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mlnx\-bf\-hugepages
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mlnx\-bf\-hugepages
is a wrapper that reads hugepage requirements from
.I /etc/mellanox/hugepages.conf
and drives
.BR doca\-hugepages (8)
to register and allocate them.
It is intended to be called by the
.B mlnx\-bf\-hugepages\-ready.service
systemd unit early in the boot process, before Open vSwitch or other DOCA
applications start.
.PP
The script supports multiple application entries and two configuration
formats (see
.BR CONFIGURATION ).
After processing all entries it calls
.B doca\-hugepages reload
once to apply the combined allocation.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration file is
.IR /etc/mellanox/hugepages.conf .
Two formats are supported:
.SS Combined format (recommended)
Each application is defined by an indexed array element:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
HUGEPAGE_APP[0]="ovs\-doca (default) 2048 2048"
HUGEPAGE_APP[1]="dpdk\-app 1048576 4"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Each value is a string of the form
.RI \(dq "app\-name size_kB num_pages" \(dq.
The application name may contain spaces.
.PP
A single\-entry shorthand (without the index) is also accepted:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
HUGEPAGE_APP="ovs\-doca (default) 2048 2048"
.fi
.RE
.SS Legacy format (single application)
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
HUGEPAGE_APP="ovs\-doca (default)"
HUGEPAGE_SIZE=2048
HUGEPAGE_NUM=2048
.fi
.RE
.PP
When neither
.I size
nor
.I num
can be parsed from the
.B HUGEPAGE_APP
value, the script falls back to
.B HUGEPAGE_SIZE
and
.BR HUGEPAGE_NUM ,
or to built\-in defaults of 2048\ kB and 2048 pages.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/mellanox/hugepages.conf
System hugepage configuration file sourced by this script.
.TP
.I /usr/sbin/doca\-hugepages
Underlying tool used for per\-application hugepage management.
.TP
.I /etc/mellanox/hugepages.d/
Per\-application JSON configurations managed by
.BR doca\-hugepages (8).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All applications configured and reload succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
One or more applications failed to configure or the final reload failed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR doca\-hugepages (8),
.BR mlnx_bf_configure_ovs (8)
